      "This pivot is grounded in action, backed by a colossal spending plan. The company is preparing for \"over $25 billion of CapEx\" in 2026 to fund this new era. The contrast is the entire story: the focus has shifted from scaling a proven, $82.1 billion auto business to funding a speculative AI future with a $25 billion checkbook, just as the old business has begun to shrink.",
      "The Quiet That Deserves A Closer Look",
      "This shift is concerning. A story pivot is one thing; a pivot away from your primary revenue engine just as it stalls is another. While the long-term vision for AI and robotics is compelling, it's a wager that will burn cash for years. Meanwhile, the company's overall net margin has collapsed from a peak of 15.5% to just 3.9%, signaling deep stress in the existing business that's supposed to fund the moonshot."
